env: env variables are given to conatiners during image run

1. this can be included as part of docker file as 
    ENV PORT =8000 #default
    --env PORT =3000 #during conatiner run time
    process.env.PORT #while reading in server.js files

2. for security reasons env variables are not baked into image as anyone can view image history
3. all the env variables are stored in .env file and are supplied during container creation
    --env-file ./.env


arg : argument variables are provided during image creation, values can be different for differnet images

1.declaration in dockerfile
    ARG DEF_PORT=80
    
2.usage during image build up
    docker build --arg-build DEF_PORT=3000 . #this overwrites def port 80 value

